<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>

<PLUGIN
  name="unraid-unzip"
  author="h4de5"
  version="2026.11.10.03"
  launch="Settings/UnraidUnzip"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/h4de5/unraid-plugins/main/unraid-unzip.plg"
  support="https://github.com/h4de5/unraid-plugins/issues"
  min="7.0.0"
  icon="file-archive-o"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[
### 2026.11.10.03

- Security: escape the archive path and target directory with `escapeHtml()` in the extract dialog (`js/unraid-unzip.js`), closing an HTML-injection (XSS) vector from a crafted archive or directory name.
- Reliability: the 7-Zip runtime is now declared as a SHA256-pinned `<FILE>` on the flash (`/boot/config/plugins/unraid-unzip/7z2605-linux-x64.tar.xz`) instead of being `curl`-downloaded to `/tmp` at every install/boot. The install script extracts it from the flash, so a cold boot with the network not yet up can no longer abort the install before `upgradepkg` runs. Matches the accepted pattern used by `zip_manager`.

### 2026.11.10.02

- Community Applications compliance: `plugins/unraid-unzip.xml` rewritten to the approved schema (single `<Plugin>` root, `<Project>`, `<Support>` -> issue tracker, `<Icon>` -> raw image URL, `<MinVer>`/`<MaxVer>`, `Tools:Utilities`); the legacy `<IconFA>` and out-of-spec `<PluginAuthor>` fields are removed.
- The install manifest `unraid-unzip.plg` is now a **tracked source file at the repo root**; its `pluginURL` is the stable raw URL (`raw.githubusercontent.com/h4de5/unraid-plugins/main/unraid-unzip.plg`), which is what the CA wrapper points at.
- `bin/generate-pages.sh`: the default `pluginURL` is the stable raw URL.
- Release pipeline: after publishing a Release it regenerates the root manifest from that build's SHA and commits it to `main`, so the raw URL always resolves to the latest release. CI asserts the committed manifest uses the raw URL.
- README / RELEASE.md / AGENTS.md updated to describe the raw-URL manifest as the canonical install source.

### 2026.11.10.01

- Repo renamed `unraid-unzip` to `unraid-plugins`; the unRAID plugin / package name is unchanged (`unraid-unzip`).
- Fix: the published `pluginURL` (and the Pages base) now point at the live `h4de5.github.io/unraid-plugins` base; the old `h4de5.github.io/unraid-unzip` base returned 404, which broke the on-box update check.
- `generate-pages.sh`: split the unRAID plugin name from the GitHub repo name so the package slot, `.plg` file and emhttp dir stay `unraid-unzip` while release assets and Pages use the new repo name.
- CA files (`ca_profile.xml`, `plugins/unraid-unzip.xml`), README, RELEASE.md, AGENTS.md and the CI/release URL checks now reference the canonical `unraid-plugins` repo.

### 2026.11.08.05

- Add Community Applications submission files: `ca_profile.xml` (repo profile) and `plugins/unraid-unzip.xml` (plugin wrapper, category Tools:Utilities).
- `.plg` support link now points to the GitHub issue tracker instead of the repo root.
- Repo-wide style: em/en dashes replaced with plain hyphens; rule added to `AGENTS.md`.

### 2026.11.08.04

- Fix: settings page no longer inlined on /Settings overview (Menu moved from `Settings` to `OtherSettings`).
- Shorten the about paragraph on the settings page.

### 2026.11.08.03

- Refactor exclude-pattern normalisation into a testable, unit-tested helper (same behaviour as 0.02).

### 2026.11.08.02

- Fix: excludes match at any archive depth; pre-fill target dir in extract dialog; shorten plugin description; prune empty staging dirs after extraction.

### 2026.11.08.01

- Settings restructured (descriptions, Advanced accordion); saved exclude list now always applied to extractions; saved passwords always tried; notifications on by default (suppressable); mobile-friendly dialog; plugin description for the plugin list.

### 2026.11.07.05

- Installation now replaces a single plugin slot instead of creating one per version; legacy slots are cleaned up.

### 2026.11.07.04

- Password list is now a plain editable textbox, shown and saved like the exclude list; removed the keep/clear mechanism.

### 2026.11.07.03

- Settings save rewritten: single API call, no /update.htm; password + exclude lists persisted directly.

### 2026.11.07.02

- Fixed settings save (relative API URL returned the HTML error page).

### 2026.11.07.01

- Dark-theme aware settings page and dialogs.
- Fixed settings page (eval'd plugin dir resolution).
- Removed the create-archive feature (extraction only).

### 2026.11.06.01

- Initial implementation.
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/unraid-unzip/unraid-unzip-2026.11.10.03-noarch-1.txz">
<URL>https://github.com/h4de5/unraid-plugins/releases/download/v2026.11.10.03/unraid-unzip-2026.11.10.03-noarch-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>d2b5ede5223540d371a5370c839ab394edbb0e1d906058e0aacbe62f6090fa67</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!-- 7-Zip runtime: kept on the flash so it is downloaded once, not at every boot -->
<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/unraid-unzip/7z2605-linux-x64.tar.xz">
<URL>https://github.com/ip7z/7zip/releases/download/26.05/7z2605-linux-x64.tar.xz</URL>
<SHA256>22cf82fcc6eb7474f1d5bb4f02c0f8ebd573a718089d6833dc30f8350a3b232e</SHA256>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
set -e
install_dir="/boot/config/plugins/unraid-unzip"
mkdir -p "$install_dir"
chmod 755 "$install_dir"

# --- 7-Zip runtime dependency (verified, from the flash) ----------------------
# The tarball is downloaded and SHA256-checked by the <FILE> element above.
sevenzip_file="7z2605-linux-x64.tar.xz"
sevenzip_sha="22cf82fcc6eb7474f1d5bb4f02c0f8ebd573a718089d6833dc30f8350a3b232e"
sevenzip_tar="$install_dir/$sevenzip_file"
if [[ ! -x /usr/bin/7zzs || "$(sha256sum /usr/bin/7zzs 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $1}')" != "$sevenzip_sha" ]]; then
  if [[ ! -f "$sevenzip_tar" ]]; then
    echo "unraid-unzip: 7-Zip tarball missing: $sevenzip_tar" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  actual="$(sha256sum "$sevenzip_tar" | awk '{print $1}')"
  if [[ "$actual" != "$sevenzip_sha" ]]; then
    echo "unraid-unzip: 7-Zip checksum mismatch" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  killall 7zzs >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  tar -xOf "$sevenzip_tar" 7zzs > /usr/bin/7zzs
  chmod 755 /usr/bin/7zzs
fi
# drop 7-Zip tarballs left by an older pin
rm -f $(ls "$install_dir"/7z*-linux-x64.tar.xz 2>/dev/null | grep -v "$sevenzip_file")
# --- end 7-Zip dependency -----------------------------------------------------

upgradepkg --install-new "$install_dir/unraid-unzip-2026.11.10.03-noarch-1.txz"

# cleanup old package versions
rm -f $(ls "$install_dir"/unraid-unzip-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v "2026.11.10.03")

echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " unraid-unzip has been installed."
echo " Version: 2026.11.10.03"
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
removepkg unraid-unzip

killall 7zzs >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
rm -f /usr/bin/7zzs
rm -f "/boot/config/plugins/unraid-unzip/7z2605-linux-x64.tar.xz"
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/unraid-unzip

# Keep user configuration and history on remove.
echo "unraid-unzip removed; configuration kept in /boot/config/plugins/unraid-unzip"
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
